== Trivia ==
* Like most of the characters that start with only soul/black (or bone, in this case) hearts, The Forgotten's starting health is listed as "-I" on the character selection screen.
* The Forgotten is Isaac's withered body.
* The Forgotten's concept is confirmed to have originally been an [https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1227014568028696581 old concept for a direct sequel to The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth].
* If his bone club is big enough, the screen will shake when he swings it. The duration of the shaking depends on how big his club is.
** {{plat|PS4}} {{plat|XboxOne}} {{plat|Switch}} The controller will also vibrate if his bone club is big enough.
* As a secret character, The Forgotten does not appear on the character select screen until unlocked.
** He shares this trait with {{C|???}}, {{C|The Lost}} and the {{C|Keeper}}.
* The Forgotten has an unused sprite in his sprite sheet of him lying down.
* The name of the achievement to unlock the Forgotten, "It's complicated," was originally the name of the achievement to unlocking {{C|The Lost}} in base Rebirth. However, since the Lost received a new unlock method in Afterbirth, this was changed.

== Bugs ==
{{Bug|Making a deal with the devil that kills The Forgotten and switching into The Soul before ending the animation will make only The Soul playable, and vice versa. If The Forgotten is no longer playable, The Soul will be locked to the range of the chain. This will effectively softlock the run unless you also have {{i|Birthright}}.}}
{{Bug|If The Forgotten obtains {{i|Brimstone}} right after the bone club is thrown (via effects like {{i|D4}} or {{r|Dice Room}} or [[debug console]]), a barrage of knives is fired instead of a brimstone ball.}}
{{Bug|If The Forgotten obtains multiple copies of {{i|Monstro's Lung}}, he will swing 5 additional bone clubs in his melee attack per copy, up to a limit of 16.}}
{{Bug|plat=PS4|dlc=a+|Very rarely, The Forgotten's head will permanently vanish when picking up his first passive item. This bug remains unfixed even after restarting the game.}}
{{Bug|Switching into The Soul and spawning enough entities will despawn the chain's links and let him fly around the room freely as if {{i|Birthright}} was obtained. This lasts until The Soul enters a different room or switches back into The Forgotten.}}

